+
+Date: 2026-09-18. Decision: **DEFERRED pending the Phase 8 product decision.**
+
+Spec entry (`15_PHASE5_IMPLEMENTATION_SPEC.md` §5.8 / doc 12): the 5.2-5.4 data endpoints
+already exist; what is missing is the product decision (is the Advanced Worker View in V1.6
+scope?) and user research; the exit gate is a usability review with the zero-visit default
+preserved.
+
+Current evidence: no product decision has been made; Kel's normal UX remains one capable
+assistant with hidden orchestration, and the workforce surfaces stay read-mostly engine-level
+(no live caller). Implementing panels now would violate the program rules "do not implement
+merely because the phase number exists" (bootstrap §30) and the spec's "no UI-first".
+
+Disposition: nothing builds. The endpoints stay available for a future decision; if the product
+decision is to ship it, re-entry is a bounded UI increment behind a setting (Advanced/Details
+only, exportable mission report), with the zero-visit default preserved.
